#!/bin/bash
# wiki-ingest-run [options] <url> — ingest a URL into the Obsidian wiki via an LLM CLI.
#
# Each ingest runs in a git worktree in /tmp. The script fetches and stages the
# verbatim raw/ file itself (curl + trafilatura, no LLM; YouTube via ytx — see
# wiki-ingest-fetch); the LLM CLI reads that archive and writes summary/, the
# analysis page, index and log; the script then commits to a branch and merges
# back to main. The merge=union gitattribute on index.md and log.md prevents
# merge conflicts, so parallel ingests are safe by design.
#
# The archive slug comes from the URL (url_slug), except for YouTube, where the
# URL's last segment is the constant "watch": there the slug comes from the
# fetched transcript's title line, so the fetch happens before the slug is
# resolved. A URL an archive already holds keeps that archive's slug regardless.
#
# The slug, and the LLM's note title, are chosen against this ingest's own
# worktree, which cannot see a parallel peer's not-yet-merged files (kata 925f).
# Two sources that land on the same slug or title both look free; the second to
# merge gets add/add conflicts. That merge is aborted at once (a content
# conflict never clears on retry), the unmerged branch is deleted, and the whole
# ingest re-runs with the original arguments from a fresh worktree off main,
# where the peer's files are visible and the slug ladder suffixes. At most two
# re-runs (WIKI_INGEST_COLLISION_RERUN counts them), so a third racing peer is
# still absorbed; after that it is exit 1 with the branch kept.
#
# The wiki has a second writer (a CI runner ingesting into a fresh clone), so
# before anything reads the checkout the script catches main up with origin/main
# (sync_with_origin): fetch, and merge origin's commit in if main lacks it, so
# the dup-check sees URLs the other writer already ingested and the worktree is
# cut from current main. It is never fatal — no origin, offline, a conflict
# (our merge aborted), a merge that will not start, or a git operation already
# in progress: one line on stderr and the ingest runs on local main. Skipped for
# --dry-run, in a collision re-run, and with WIKI_INGEST_NO_SYNC=1. A rejected
# push catches up the same way (push_with_sync).
#
# Two modes, chosen by whether topics.md exists in the wiki (the gate is the
# file, not a flag, because the hourly job runs this script from the working
# tree and a wiki must switch over at exactly the commit that lands topics.md):
#
#   topics mode (topics.md present): the analysis page is note/<Title>.md, the
#     summary's frontmatter carries a topics: block list of one or two slugs
#     from topics.md, and topic/ is reserved for compiled pages that only
#     wiki-compile writes. The guard requires exactly one NEW note/ page (a
#     modified one only on a --force re-ingest of the same source), rejects
#     any topic/ write and any edit to topics.md, and repairs topics: with
#     wiki-meta normalize-topics rather than rejecting a metadata slip.
#   legacy mode (no topics.md): the analysis page is topic/<Title>.md and the
#     prompts and guard are unchanged from before topics existed.
#
# See docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-11-fixed-topics-design.md.
#
# Options:
#   --repo            GitHub repo deep-analysis mode (shallow-clones the repo,
#                     uses the repo-analysis prompt)
#   --content FILE    pre-fetched content (surf fallback): FILE becomes the
#                     verbatim source (extracted if it is HTML, else used as-is)
#                     staged to raw/<slug>.md; the script does not fetch the URL
#   --force           skip the duplicate check; tell the LLM this is a re-ingest
#   --note TEXT       append TEXT to the LLM prompt (source-type hints, etc.)
#   --date YYYY-MM-DD override today's date (default: date '+%Y-%m-%d')
#   --dry-run         plumbing test: skip the LLM; write a marker file, merge the
#                     ingest branch into a THROWAWAY branch created from main
#                     (never into main), verify, clean up. Leaves zero trace.
#   --summary-only    BACKFILL an existing source: the argument is a slug naming
#                     an existing raw/<slug>.md, or a URL, which is resolved to
#                     whichever archive actually holds it.
#                     Nothing is fetched or cloned; the LLM reads that archive
#                     and writes ONLY summary/<slug>.md (with a topics: list in
#                     topics mode). The analysis page, index.md and log.md are
#                     left alone — the source is already indexed and logged,
#                     this only fills in a missing precis.
#
# Exit codes:
#   0  ingested (or dry-run OK, or summary backfilled)
#   2  duplicate — already ingested (use --force to re-ingest)
#   3  no changes — fetch likely failed (orchestrator should retry with surf)
#   5  merged into the local main but not pushed to origin, with
#      WIKI_INGEST_REQUIRE_PUSH=1 (for a throwaway clone, e.g. CI). Without it
#      a failed push is still exit 0, reported as push-failed. A rejected push
#      is first retried after fetching origin/main and merging it into main
#      (3 pushes); a conflict with origin aborts that merge and keeps the
#      local commit.
#   64 usage error
#   1  other failure — including, for --summary-only, a missing raw/<slug>.md,
#      an LLM that wrote nothing, or one that wrote outside summary/; for an
#      ingest, a slug ladder with no free candidate left; and, in topics mode,
#      an LLM that wrote under topic/, edited topics.md, or staged anything
#      other than exactly one new note/ page; and a slug/title collision with
#      peer ingests that persisted through both automatic re-runs
#   A collision re-run exits with the re-run's own code (so a peer that turns
#   out to have ingested the SAME URL makes it 2, duplicate).
#
# Single call (WIKI_INGEST_MODE=single; default agentic): a fresh topics-mode
# article ingest makes ONE chat-completions request through wiki-llm instead of
# an agentic CLI session. The script inlines the archive, the topics table, all
# note/topic titles and the nearest notes (wiki-neighbours), writes summary/,
# note/, the index.md entry and the log.md line from the reply, and then the
# same guard, topics repair, commit and merge run. --repo, --summary-only,
# --verbatim-only, --force and legacy mode always use the agentic path.
# Needs WIKI_LLM_BASE_URL and a key (wiki-llm --help). WIKI_INGEST_MODEL
# (default deepseek-4.1-flash-background), WIKI_INGEST_EFFORT (default low),
# WIKI_INGEST_MAX_TOKENS (default 16000), WIKI_LLM (default wiki-llm beside this
# script).
#
# Targets bash 3.2 (macOS /bin/bash). Runs non-interactively (launchd-safe).

set -eu

# The original argv, before option parsing consumes it: a slug/title collision
# re-runs the whole script with exactly these arguments (see the main merge).
ORIG_ARGV=("$@")

WIKI="${WIKI_PATH:-}"
if [ -z "$WIKI" ] || [ ! -d "$WIKI" ]; then
  echo "wiki-ingest-run: set WIKI_PATH to your wiki directory (currently: '${WIKI_PATH:-unset}'). Run wiki-ingest-setup first if you haven't created it." >&2
  exit 64
fi
CLI="${WIKI_INGEST_CLI:-claude}"
SCRIPT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)"
# Every agentic LLM session goes through wiki-agent, which turns --tools and
# --context into $CLI's own flags (claude or pi dialect).
AGENT="$SCRIPT_DIR/wiki-agent"
[ -x "$AGENT" ] || { echo "wiki-ingest-run: wiki-agent not found beside me" >&2; exit 64; }
INGEST_MODE="${WIKI_INGEST_MODE:-agentic}"
case "$INGEST_MODE" in
  agentic) ;;
  single)
    LLM="${WIKI_LLM:-$SCRIPT_DIR/wiki-llm}"
    if [ ! -x "$LLM" ] || [ ! -x "$SCRIPT_DIR/wiki-neighbours" ]; then
      echo "wiki-ingest-run: WIKI_INGEST_MODE=single needs $LLM and $SCRIPT_DIR/wiki-neighbours" >&2
      exit 64
    fi ;;
  *) echo "wiki-ingest-run: WIKI_INGEST_MODE must be agentic or single, not '$INGEST_MODE'" >&2; exit 64 ;;
esac
SINGLE_SCRATCH=""

# The merge, push, and branch reaping below all assume the wiki checkout is on
# main. If it was left on another branch, ingests would silently land there.
WIKI_HEAD="$(git -C "$WIKI" rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD)"
if [ "$WIKI_HEAD" != "main" ]; then
  echo "wiki-ingest-run: wiki checkout is on '$WIKI_HEAD', not main — refusing to ingest" >&2
  exit 1
fi

# --- Catching up with origin/main ----------------------------------------------
# The wiki has more than one writer (this Mac's clone and a CI runner's fresh
# clone), so origin/main moves on without us. Two places merge it into the live
# checkout: sync_with_origin at the start of an ingest, and push_with_sync after
# a rejected push. Both use the helpers below, under one set of rules: merge the
# fetched SHA (not the ref, which a parallel ingest's fetch may move under us);
# abort only a merge whose MERGE_HEAD is exactly that SHA (a failed `git merge`
# may be a PEER's merge in progress, and aborting that loses its ingest — see
# merge_with_retry); and treat a merge that never started (index.lock, a local
# edit in the way) as retryable, not as a conflict.

# The git operations that leave the checkout mid-flight, space-separated (empty
# when none). --absolute-git-dir, not --git-dir: the latter is relative to this
# script's cwd, and the check silently never fires.
inprogress_ops() {
  local gd st ops=""
  gd=$(git -C "$WIKI" rev-parse --absolute-git-dir 2>/dev/null || true)
  [ -n "$gd" ] || return 0
  for st in MERGE_HEAD CHERRY_PICK_HEAD REVERT_HEAD rebase-merge rebase-apply sequencer; do
    if [ -e "$gd/$st" ]; then ops="$ops $st"; fi
  done
  printf '%s' "$ops"
}

# Fetch origin's main. 0 with ORIGIN_SHA set; 1 with SYNC_WHY saying why not.
# Explicit refspec: a CI checkout may carry a narrowed fetch config, and the
# bare `fetch origin main` then updates only FETCH_HEAD.
ORIGIN_SHA=""
SYNC_WHY=""
fetch_origin_main() {
  ORIGIN_SHA=""
  if ! git -C "$WIKI" remote get-url origin >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    SYNC_WHY="no origin remote"; return 1
  fi
  if ! GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 git -C "$WIKI" fetch --quiet origin "+refs/heads/main:refs/remotes/origin/main" 2>/dev/null; then
    SYNC_WHY="fetch from origin failed"; return 1
  fi
  if ! ORIGIN_SHA=$(git -C "$WIKI" rev-parse -q --verify "refs/remotes/origin/main^{commit}" 2>/dev/null); then
    ORIGIN_SHA=""; SYNC_WHY="origin has no main branch"; return 1
  fi
  return 0
}

# merge_origin_sha <message> [ff-only] — merge ORIGIN_SHA into main, once.
# 0 merged; 2 a content conflict, our merge aborted (SYNC_WHY names the paths);
# 3 the merge never started, nothing to abort — the caller may wait and retry.
merge_origin_sha() {
  local msg="$1" ok=1 paths
  if [ "${2:-}" = ff-only ]; then
    git -C "$WIKI" merge --ff-only "$ORIGIN_SHA" >/dev/null 2>&1 && ok=0
  else
    git -C "$WIKI" merge "$ORIGIN_SHA" --no-edit -m "$msg" >/dev/null 2>&1 && ok=0
  fi
  [ "$ok" -eq 0 ] && return 0
  if [ "$(git -C "$WIKI" rev-parse -q --verify MERGE_HEAD 2>/dev/null)" = "$ORIGIN_SHA" ]; then
    paths=$(git -C "$WIKI" -c core.quotePath=false diff --name-only --diff-filter=U 2>/dev/null | tr '\n' ' ')
    SYNC_WHY="origin/main conflicts with main on: ${paths% }"
    git -C "$WIKI" merge --abort 2>/dev/null || true
    return 2
  fi
  return 3
}

# Catch main up with origin/main before the dup-check and the worktree, so a
# URL another writer already ingested is seen as a duplicate and the worktree
# is cut from current main. Never fatal: whatever goes wrong, one line on
# stderr and the ingest proceeds on local main exactly as it would have.
# A tree with uncommitted tracked edits (Obsidian) is only ever fast-forwarded:
# a fast-forward cannot conflict, so nothing is aborted over those edits; a
# diverged main with a dirty tree is left for push_with_sync, which runs after
# the auto-commit.
sync_with_origin() {
  local ops mrc tries=1 mode=""
  ops=$(inprogress_ops)
  if [ -n "$ops" ]; then
    echo "wiki-ingest-run: not catching up with origin/main: a git operation is in progress ($ops)" >&2
    return 0
  fi
  if ! fetch_origin_main; then
    echo "wiki-ingest-run: not catching up with origin/main: $SYNC_WHY — ingesting on local main" >&2
    return 0
  fi
  git -C "$WIKI" merge-base --is-ancestor "$ORIGIN_SHA" main 2>/dev/null && return 0
  if ! git -C "$WIKI" diff --quiet HEAD -- 2>/dev/null; then
    if ! git -C "$WIKI" merge-base --is-ancestor main "$ORIGIN_SHA" 2>/dev/null; then
      echo "wiki-ingest-run: not catching up with origin/main: main has diverged and the tree has uncommitted edits — left to the push" >&2
      return 0
    fi
    mode=ff-only
  fi
  while [ "$tries" -le 3 ]; do
    merge_origin_sha "Merge origin/main into main before ingest" $mode && mrc=0 || mrc=$?
    case "$mrc" in
      0) echo "wiki-ingest-run: caught up with origin/main ($ORIGIN_SHA)" >&2; return 0 ;;
      2) echo "wiki-ingest-run: not catching up with origin/main: $SYNC_WHY — merge aborted, ingesting on local main" >&2; return 0 ;;
    esac
    sleep 1
    tries=$((tries + 1))
  done
  echo "wiki-ingest-run: not catching up with origin/main: the merge would not start (index.lock or a local edit in the way) — ingesting on local main" >&2
  return 0
}

usage() {
  echo "usage: wiki-ingest-run [--repo] [--content FILE] [--force] [--note TEXT] [--date YYYY-MM-DD] [--dry-run] [--verbatim-only] <url>" >&2
  echo "       wiki-ingest-run --summary-only <slug|url>   # backfill summary/<slug>.md from an existing raw/<slug>.md" >&2
  echo "The analysis page goes to note/<Title>.md with a topics: list on the summary when the wiki has a topics.md, else to topic/<Title>.md (legacy)." >&2
  exit 64
}

# Deterministic slug from a URL: last meaningful path segment, lowercased,
# non-alphanumerics → hyphens; fall back to the host. Same input → same slug,
# so raw/<slug>.md and summary/<slug>.md always agree.
#
# YouTube is the one exception: youtube.com/watch?v=ID has the constant last
# segment "watch", so resolve_slug is handed title_slug of the fetched
# transcript instead (see is_youtube_url / title_slug below). Kata 4gpv is the
# general form of the query-string problem; this does not attempt it.
url_slug() {
  local u="$1" seg host
  u="${u%%\?*}"; u="${u%%#*}"; u="${u#http://}"; u="${u#https://}"; u="${u#www.}"
  u="${u%/}"
  host="${u%%/*}"
  seg="${u##*/}"
  case "$seg" in
    ""|"$host") seg="$host" ;;
  esac
  seg=$(printf '%s' "$seg" | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]' | tr -c 'a-z0-9' '-')
  seg="${seg##-}"; seg="${seg%%-}"
  [ -n "$seg" ] || seg="source"
  printf '%s' "$seg"
}

# is_youtube_url <url> — host is youtube.com, any *.youtube.com, or youtu.be.
# A copy of the helper in bin/wiki-ingest-fetch, which routes these
# URLs through ytx; the two MUST agree, or a URL could be fetched as a
# transcript but slugged as "watch" (or the reverse).
is_youtube_url() {
  local u="$1"
  u="${u#http://}"; u="${u#https://}"
  case "$u" in
    youtube.com/*|*.youtube.com/*|youtu.be/*) return 0 ;;
    *) return 1 ;;
  esac
}

# title_slug <body> — slug of the body's first "# " heading line, or the empty
# string when there is none. Same rules as url_slug (lowercase, non-
# alphanumerics → hyphens, trimmed), with hyphen runs squeezed and an 80-char
# cap that cuts back to the last hyphen if that leaves more than 40 chars —
# mirroring ytx's Slugify (internal/publish/publish.go) so an archive's slug
# matches the name ytx itself would have given the transcript.
title_slug() {
  local t s cut
  t=$(printf '%s\n' "$1" | sed -n 's/^# //p' | head -1)
  [ -n "$t" ] || return 0
  s=$(printf '%s' "$t" | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]' | tr -cs 'a-z0-9' '-')
  s="${s##-}"; s="${s%%-}"
  if [ ${#s} -gt 80 ]; then
    s="${s:0:80}"
    cut="${s%-*}"
    if [ ${#cut} -gt 40 ]; then s="$cut"; fi
    s="${s%%-}"
  fi
  printf '%s' "$s"
}

# THE SUFFIX SCHEME LIVES HERE AND NOWHERE ELSE.
#
# When a DIFFERENT source already owns the base slug, resolve_slug disambiguates
# by appending this token (cloudflare-os -> cloudflare-os-github). The token's
# SHAPE is a taste call about how the vault reads, not a correctness property:
# the collision mechanism below works with any non-empty token. Change the body
# of this one function to change the scheme; nothing else knows what it means.
#
# Current scheme: the canonical host minus its final dot-label.
#   github.com -> github    blog.cloudflare.com -> blog-cloudflare
slug_disambiguator() {
  local u="$1" host tok
  u="${u%%\?*}"; u="${u%%#*}"; u="${u#http://}"; u="${u#https://}"; u="${u#www.}"
  host="${u%%/*}"
  host=$(printf '%s' "$host" | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')
  tok="${host%.*}"
  [ -n "$tok" ] || tok="$host"
  tok=$(printf '%s' "$tok" | tr -c 'a-z0-9' '-')
  tok="${tok##-}"; tok="${tok%%-}"
  [ -n "$tok" ] || tok="alt"
  printf '%s' "$tok"
}

# owning_slug <wiki-or-worktree> <url> — print the slug of the archive that
# ALREADY holds this URL, if exactly one does.
#
# Returns 0 and prints the slug; 1 when no archive holds it; 2 when the answer
# is ambiguous or dupcheck itself failed. 2 is never a guess: guessing here
# either duplicates a source or backfills the wrong one.
#
# The comparison is delegated to wiki-ingest-dupcheck rather than reimplemented
# here. dupcheck already folds http/https, leading www., trailing /, #fragment
# and trailing .git; a second copy of that logic would drift, and the drift
# failure mode is exactly the re-ingest-duplication this exists to prevent.
owning_slug() {
  local w="$1" url="$2" dup_out drc names count
  if [ ! -x "$SCRIPT_DIR/wiki-ingest-dupcheck" ]; then
    echo "wiki-ingest-run: $SCRIPT_DIR/wiki-ingest-dupcheck missing or not executable — cannot tell a re-ingest from a slug collision" >&2
    return 2
  fi
  set +e
  dup_out=$(WIKI_PATH="$w" "$SCRIPT_DIR/wiki-ingest-dupcheck" "$url" 2>/dev/null)
  drc=$?
  set -e
  case "$drc" in
    1) return 1 ;;  # nothing holds it
    0) : ;;
    *) echo "wiki-ingest-run: dupcheck failed (rc=$drc) for $url — refusing to guess a slug" >&2
       return 2 ;;
  esac
  # Un-indented output lines are file paths; the indented ones are title/date
  # detail. raw/<s>.md and summary/<s>.md both matching is one slug, not two.
  names=$(printf '%s\n' "$dup_out" | sed -n 's|^[^[:space:]].*/\([^/]*\)\.md$|\1|p' | sort -u)
  count=$(printf '%s\n' "$names" | sed '/^$/d' | wc -l | tr -d ' ')
  if [ "$count" -eq 1 ]; then
    printf '%s' "$names"
    return 0
  fi
  echo "wiki-ingest-run: $url is held by $count archives ($(printf '%s' "$names" | tr '\n' ' ')) — refusing to guess which one it belongs to" >&2
  return 2
}

# resolve_slug <worktree> <url> [base] — the slug this URL should be archived
# under. The optional third argument replaces url_slug as the base candidate
# (YouTube hands in title_slug of the transcript); empty means url_slug.
#
# Step 1: if an archive already holds this URL, that IS its slug. This is the
# --force re-ingest path and it must update in place; suffixing here would turn
# every re-ingest into a duplicate, which is worse than the collision being
# fixed. It also finds hand-chosen slugs no rule would generate — which is why
# it runs before, and regardless of, any base override: a re-ingest of a
# hand-renamed YouTube archive keeps the hand-chosen name, not the title's.
#
# Step 2: otherwise this is a genuinely different source that happens to share a
# last path segment. Walk a bounded ladder and take the first candidate no
# archive owns. Both tiers are checked because migrated content can have a
# summary/ with no raw/, and handing out that slug would attach this source's
# archive to someone else's precis.
#
# Exhausting the ladder is exit 1 with the candidates named — never a silent
# overwrite. (Exit codes 2 and 3 are reserved contract values.)
resolve_slug() {
  local wt="$1" url="$2" base="${3:-}" own orc tok cand i tried
  set +e; own=$(owning_slug "$wt" "$url"); orc=$?; set -e
  case "$orc" in
    0) printf '%s' "$own"; return 0 ;;
    2) return 1 ;;  # message already printed
  esac

  [ -n "$base" ] || base=$(url_slug "$url")
  tok=$(slug_disambiguator "$url")
  cand="$base"
  tried=""
  i=0
  while :; do
    if [ ! -e "$wt/raw/$cand.md" ] && [ ! -e "$wt/summary/$cand.md" ]; then
      printf '%s' "$cand"
      return 0
    fi
    tried="$tried $cand"
    i=$((i + 1))
    if [ "$i" -eq 1 ]; then
      cand="$base-$tok"
    elif [ "$i" -le 9 ]; then
      cand="$base-$tok-$i"
    else
      echo "wiki-ingest-run: no free slug for $url — every candidate is taken by another source:$tried" >&2
      echo "wiki-ingest-run: refusing to overwrite an existing archive; rename one by hand or widen the ladder" >&2
      return 1
    fi
  done
}

REPO_MODE=0
CONTENT_FILE=""
FORCE=0
DRY_RUN=0
VERBATIM_ONLY=0
SUMMARY_ONLY=0
NOTE=""
INGEST_DATE="$(date '+%Y-%m-%d')"
INGEST_URL=""

while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
  case "$1" in
    --repo)    REPO_MODE=1; shift ;;
    --content) [ $# -ge 2 ] || usage; CONTENT_FILE="$2"; shift 2 ;;
    --force)   FORCE=1; shift ;;
    --note)    [ $# -ge 2 ] || usage; NOTE="$2"; shift 2 ;;
    --date)    [ $# -ge 2 ] || usage; INGEST_DATE="$2"; shift 2 ;;
    --dry-run) DRY_RUN=1; shift ;;
    --verbatim-only) VERBATIM_ONLY=1; shift ;;
    --summary-only)  SUMMARY_ONLY=1; shift ;;
    --)        shift; [ $# -eq 1 ] || usage; INGEST_URL="$1"; shift ;;
    -*)        usage ;;
    *)         [ -z "$INGEST_URL" ] || usage; INGEST_URL="$1"; shift ;;
  esac
done
[ -n "$INGEST_URL" ] || usage

if [ -n "$CONTENT_FILE" ] && [ ! -r "$CONTENT_FILE" ]; then
  echo "wiki-ingest-run: --content file not readable: $CONTENT_FILE" >&2
  exit 64
fi

# --- --summary-only: resolve the slug and prove the source exists -------------

# Backfill reads an existing archive; fetching, cloning, dry-run plumbing and
# the verbatim verdict pass all belong to a fresh ingest. Checked before the
# catch-up below, so a usage error never touches the checkout.
if [ "$SUMMARY_ONLY" -eq 1 ]; then
  if [ "$REPO_MODE" -eq 1 ] || [ -n "$CONTENT_FILE" ] || [ "$DRY_RUN" -eq 1 ] || [ "$VERBATIM_ONLY" -eq 1 ]; then
    echo "wiki-ingest-run: --summary-only cannot be combined with --repo, --content, --dry-run or --verbatim-only" >&2
    exit 64
  fi
fi

# --- Catch up with origin/main ----------------------------------------------
# Before anything reads the checkout: --summary-only's slug resolution, the
# dup-check and the worktree all look at local main. Skipped for --dry-run
# (which must leave no trace, and never touches main), in a collision re-run
# (its parent caught up seconds ago, and the peer it collided with is local),
# and with WIKI_INGEST_NO_SYNC=1.
if [ "$DRY_RUN" -ne 1 ] && [ "${WIKI_INGEST_NO_SYNC:-0}" != 1 ] \
   && [ "${WIKI_INGEST_COLLISION_RERUN:-0}" = 0 ]; then
  sync_with_origin
fi

SUMMARY_SLUG=""
if [ "$SUMMARY_ONLY" -eq 1 ]; then
  # Slugs are [a-z0-9-] by construction (see url_slug); anything else is a URL.
  # A URL is resolved to the archive that actually HOLDS it, not to whatever
  # url_slug derives: once slugs can carry a collision suffix, the derived name
  # may belong to an entirely different source and backfilling it would
  # overwrite that source's precis. A bare slug is used as given, as before.
  case "$INGEST_URL" in
    *[!a-z0-9-]*)
      set +e; SUMMARY_SLUG=$(owning_slug "$WIKI" "$INGEST_URL"); orc=$?; set -e
      case "$orc" in
        0) : ;;
        1) echo "wiki-ingest-run: --summary-only: no archive in $WIKI holds $INGEST_URL" >&2; exit 1 ;;
        *) exit 1 ;;  # owning_slug already explained why
      esac
      ;;
    *)  SUMMARY_SLUG="$INGEST_URL" ;;
  esac
  if [ ! -f "$WIKI/raw/$SUMMARY_SLUG.md" ]; then
    echo "wiki-ingest-run: --summary-only: no such source raw/$SUMMARY_SLUG.md in $WIKI" >&2
    exit 1
  fi
fi

# --- Reap stale state from previous runs ------------------------------------

git -C "$WIKI" worktree prune

# Delete fully-merged ingest-* branches (leftovers from clean runs).
git -C "$WIKI" branch --merged main --list 'ingest-*' | sed 's/^[*+ ]*//' | \
while read -r b; do
  [ -n "$b" ] || continue
  git -C "$WIKI" branch -d "$b" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
done

# Force-delete ingest-* branches whose tip commit is older than 7 days.
# Unmerged ingest branches are retryable failures; after a week they're junk.
now=$(date +%s)
week_ago=$((now - 7 * 24 * 3600))
git -C "$WIKI" branch --list 'ingest-*' | sed 's/^[*+ ]*//' | \
while read -r b; do
  [ -n "$b" ] || continue
  tip=$(git -C "$WIKI" log -1 --format=%ct "$b" 2>/dev/null) || continue
  case "$tip" in ''|*[!0-9]*) continue ;; esac
  if [ "$tip" -lt "$week_ago" ]; then
    git -C "$WIKI" branch -D "$b" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
  fi
done

# --- Duplicate check ----------------------------------------------------------

# --summary-only is a backfill of an already-ingested source, so the duplicate
# it would find is exactly the source it is meant to work on.
if [ "$FORCE" -ne 1 ] && [ "$SUMMARY_ONLY" -ne 1 ]; then
  if [ ! -x "$SCRIPT_DIR/wiki-ingest-dupcheck" ]; then
    echo "wiki-ingest-run: $SCRIPT_DIR/wiki-ingest-dupcheck missing or not executable — refusing to ingest without duplicate check (use --force to override)" >&2
    exit 1
  fi
  set +e; dup_out=$("$SCRIPT_DIR/wiki-ingest-dupcheck" "$INGEST_URL"); drc=$?; set -e
  case "$drc" in
    0) echo "DUPLICATE — already ingested:"; echo "$dup_out"; exit 2 ;;
    1) : ;;  # clean — proceed
    *) echo "wiki-ingest-run: dupcheck failed (rc=$drc) for $INGEST_URL — refusing to risk a duplicate" >&2; exit 1 ;;
  esac
fi

# --- Worktree setup -----------------------------------------------------------

BRANCH="ingest-$(date +%s)-$$-$RANDOM"
WT="/tmp/wiki-$BRANCH"
CLONE_DIR=""
THROWAWAY=""
TWT=""

cleanup() {
  [ -n "$SINGLE_SCRATCH" ] && rm -rf "$SINGLE_SCRATCH"
  git -C "$WIKI" worktree remove --force "$WT" 2>/dev/null || true
  if [ -n "$TWT" ]; then
    git -C "$WIKI" worktree remove --force "$TWT" 2>/dev/null || true
  fi
  if [ -n "$THROWAWAY" ]; then
    git -C "$WIKI" branch -D "$THROWAWAY" 2>/dev/null || true
  fi
  if [ "$DRY_RUN" -eq 1 ]; then
    # Dry-run branches were only merged into the throwaway branch, so -d
    # would refuse; they must never survive.
    git -C "$WIKI" branch -D "$BRANCH" 2>/dev/null || true
  else
    # -d only deletes if merged: a failed ingest's branch survives for retry
    # (and is reaped after 7 days).
    git -C "$WIKI" branch -d "$BRANCH" 2>/dev/null || true
  fi
  if [ -n "$CLONE_DIR" ]; then
    rm -rf "$CLONE_DIR"
  fi
}
trap cleanup EXIT

# Merge $BRANCH into the checkout at $1, retrying up to 5 times. Parallel
# ingests contend on index.lock — abort, sleep, retry handles that.
# Abort only a merge that is OURS. `git merge` also fails before it starts, when
# a peer ingest is mid-merge in the same checkout; an abort then resets the
# PEER's merge. The peer's commit still lands, the working tree is left behind
# it, and the next ingest auto-commits the peer's files as deletions — a whole
# ingest lost after it exited 0 (2026-09-20). Skipping the abort just waits the
# peer out.
#
# Returns 0 merged, 1 out of retries, 3 slug/title collision: OUR merge stopped
# on add/add paths (named in MERGE_COLLISIONS), meaning a peer that merged first
# created a file this ingest also created. That is a content conflict, so it is
# aborted and returned at once instead of retried. Detected from the index
# stages (ls-files -u) rather than `status --porcelain`'s AA, which is the same
# condition but C-quotes paths containing a space — and note titles have them:
# add/add is the one unmerged state with no stage 1 (no common ancestor) and
# both stages 2 and 3.
MERGE_COLLISIONS=""
merge_with_retry() {
  local dir="$1" attempt=1 ours
  ours=$(git -C "$dir" rev-parse -q --verify "$BRANCH^{commit}" 2>/dev/null || true)
  while [ "$attempt" -le 5 ]; do
    if git -C "$dir" merge "$BRANCH" --no-edit; then
      return 0
    fi
    if [ -n "$ours" ] && [ "$(git -C "$dir" rev-parse -q --verify MERGE_HEAD 2>/dev/null)" = "$ours" ]; then
      MERGE_COLLISIONS=$(git -C "$dir" -c core.quotePath=false ls-files -u 2>/dev/null | awk -F'\t' '
        { split($1, f, " "); st[$2] = st[$2] f[3] }
        END { for (p in st) if (st[p] !~ /1/ && st[p] ~ /2/ && st[p] ~ /3/) print p }' | sort)
      git -C "$dir" merge --abort 2>/dev/null || true
      [ -z "$MERGE_COLLISIONS" ] || return 3
    fi
    sleep 3
    attempt=$((attempt + 1))
  done
  return 1
}

# --repo mode: shallow-clone the repo (structure and code, not full history).
if [ "$REPO_MODE" -eq 1 ] && [ "$DRY_RUN" -ne 1 ]; then
  case "$INGEST_URL" in
    *github.com/*) : ;;
    *) echo "wiki-ingest-run: --repo requires a github.com/<owner>/<repo> URL, got: $INGEST_URL" >&2; exit 64 ;;
  esac
  repo_path="${INGEST_URL#*github.com/}"
  repo_path="${repo_path%%\?*}"
  repo_path="${repo_path%%#*}"
  repo_path="${repo_path%/}"
  repo_path="${repo_path%.git}"
  case "$repo_path" in
    */*) : ;;
    *) echo "wiki-ingest-run: cannot derive owner/repo from URL: $INGEST_URL" >&2; exit 64 ;;
  esac
  OWNER="${repo_path%%/*}"
  REPO="${repo_path#*/}"
  REPO="${REPO%%/*}"
  if [ -z "$OWNER" ] || [ -z "$REPO" ]; then
    echo "wiki-ingest-run: cannot derive owner/repo from URL: $INGEST_URL" >&2
    exit 64
  fi
  # Unique suffix: two concurrent ingests of the same repo must not share a
  # clone dir. Clone the reconstructed canonical URL, never the raw input —
  # deep links (/tree/..., ?tab=...) would fail the clone, and raw input in a
  # clone target is an ext::/upload-pack command-injection surface.
  CLONE_DIR="/tmp/repo-$OWNER--$REPO-$$-$RANDOM"
  rm -rf "$CLONE_DIR"
  GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 git clone --depth 1 "https://github.com/$OWNER/$REPO" "$CLONE_DIR"
fi

git -C "$WIKI" worktree add "$WT" -b "$BRANCH" main
mkdir -p "$WT/raw" "$WT/summary" "$WT/topic"

# Topics mode is decided by the WORKTREE's topics.md — a fresh checkout of main
# — so the mode flips at exactly the commit that lands the file, for every
# ingest after it and none before it. wiki-meta is how the topic table is read
# and how topics: is repaired; without it the guard cannot run, so fail before
# spending an LLM call rather than after.
TOPICS_MODE=0
if [ -f "$WT/topics.md" ]; then
  TOPICS_MODE=1
  mkdir -p "$WT/note"
  if [ ! -x "$SCRIPT_DIR/wiki-meta" ]; then
    echo "wiki-ingest-run: $WIKI has topics.md but $SCRIPT_DIR/wiki-meta is missing or not executable — cannot read or validate topics" >&2
    exit 1
  fi
fi

# Stage the verbatim source deterministically (dry-run skips this;
# --summary-only skips it too — its raw/<slug>.md is already in the wiki).
SLUG=""
if [ "$SUMMARY_ONLY" -eq 1 ]; then
  SLUG="$SUMMARY_SLUG"
elif [ "$DRY_RUN" -ne 1 ]; then
  # The body is fetched BEFORE the slug is resolved: for YouTube the slug comes
  # from the transcript's title line, which only exists once ytx has run. None
  # of the three branches below write into the worktree, so the slug is still
  # resolved against a fresh checkout of main with nothing staged in it.
  FETCH="$SCRIPT_DIR/wiki-ingest-fetch"
  if [ ! -x "$FETCH" ]; then
    echo "wiki-ingest-run: $FETCH missing or not executable" >&2
    exit 1
  fi
  body=""
  if [ "$REPO_MODE" -eq 1 ]; then
    # Repo verbatim = the README (first match, case-insensitive). A repo with no
    # README still cloned fine (real content) — use a placeholder so it isn't
    # misread as a failed fetch and routed to surf.
    readme=$(find "$CLONE_DIR" -maxdepth 1 -iname 'readme*' 2>/dev/null | head -1)
    if [ -n "$readme" ]; then
      body=$(cat "$readme")
    else
      body="# $INGEST_URL

(No README found in the repository; see the topic page's analysis of the cloned source.)"
    fi
  elif [ -n "$CONTENT_FILE" ]; then
    # surf grab (already text/markdown) — extract if it is HTML, else pass through.
    if head -c 200 "$CONTENT_FILE" | grep -qi '<html\|<!doctype'; then
      # set +e around the substitution: the helper exits 3 on empty extraction;
      # under set -e a bare assignment would abort here. Capture the code so we
      # can tell "empty page" (3) from a real helper error (1) below.
      set +e; body=$("$FETCH" --file "$CONTENT_FILE"); frc=$?; set -e
    else
      body=$(cat "$CONTENT_FILE")
    fi
  else
    set +e; body=$("$FETCH" "$INGEST_URL"); frc=$?; set -e
  fi

  # Helper exit 1 is a real error (e.g. trafilatura not installed) — fail loudly
  # rather than masquerading as "no content" and silently routing every URL to
  # surf. Exit 3 (empty) and 0 (content) both fall through to the length check.
  # The helper's stderr is left alone on purpose: it carries the one line that
  # says WHY (ytx missing, ytx failed, an override that does not resolve); the
  # helper already silences curl's and trafilatura's own noise.
  if [ "${frc:-0}" -eq 1 ]; then
    echo "wiki-ingest-run: fetch helper error for $INGEST_URL (see the wiki-ingest-fetch line above)" >&2
    exit 1
  fi

  # Empty extraction = nothing to archive → fetch failure → exit 3 (→ surf).
  trimmed=$(printf '%s' "$body" | tr -d '[:space:]')
  if [ ${#trimmed} -lt 40 ]; then
    echo "NO CONTENT — fetch/extract empty for $INGEST_URL"
    exit 3
  fi

  # Resolved against the WORKTREE, which is a fresh checkout of main, and before
  # anything is written into it: an unrelated source sharing this URL's last
  # path segment must not have its raw/ and summary/ silently overwritten.
  # YouTube's last segment is the constant "watch", so its base candidate is the
  # transcript title instead (also for --content when the file starts with a
  # "# Title" line); an empty title falls back to url_slug as for any other URL.
  slug_base=""
  if is_youtube_url "$INGEST_URL"; then
    slug_base=$(title_slug "$body")
  fi
  set +e; SLUG=$(resolve_slug "$WT" "$INGEST_URL" "$slug_base"); rrc=$?; set -e
  [ "$rrc" -eq 0 ] || exit 1

  # Write the verbatim archive: minimal frontmatter (url is what dup-check needs)
  # + the exact extracted body. The LLM must NOT rewrite this file.
  {
    printf -- '---\n'
    printf 'url: %s\n' "$INGEST_URL"
    printf 'date_fetched: %s\n' "$INGEST_DATE"
    printf -- '---\n\n'
    printf '%s\n' "$body"
  } > "$WT/raw/$SLUG.md"
fi

# --- Dry run: exercise the commit + merge plumbing, never touching main -------

if [ "$DRY_RUN" -eq 1 ]; then
  echo "dry-run marker for $INGEST_URL" > "$WT/raw/_dryrun-$BRANCH.md"
  git -C "$WT" add -A
  git -C "$WT" commit --quiet -m "Dry-run ingest test: $INGEST_URL" \
    --author="wiki-ingest <noreply@wiki-ingest>"

  THROWAWAY="throwaway-$BRANCH"
  TWT="/tmp/wiki-$THROWAWAY"
  git -C "$WIKI" worktree add "$TWT" -b "$THROWAWAY" main

  # The marker's name is branch-unique and nothing else is staged, so a
  # collision (rc 3) cannot arise here; every failure stays a failure.
  if ! merge_with_retry "$TWT"; then
    echo "DRY-RUN FAILED: merge into throwaway branch failed for $INGEST_URL" >&2
    exit 1
  fi
  if [ ! -f "$TWT/raw/_dryrun-$BRANCH.md" ]; then
    echo "DRY-RUN FAILED: marker file missing after merge into throwaway branch" >&2
    exit 1
  fi
  echo "DRY-RUN OK: $INGEST_URL (branch $BRANCH merged into $THROWAWAY, marker verified, cleaning up)"
  exit 0  # trap removes both worktrees and both branches
fi

# --- Build prompt extras -------------------------------------------------------

EXTRA_NOTES=""
if [ "$FORCE" -eq 1 ] && [ "$TOPICS_MODE" -eq 1 ]; then
  EXTRA_NOTES="This is a re-ingest — update the existing summary/$SLUG.md and the existing note whose source footer cites raw/$SLUG (find it with grep under note/), do not duplicate them. Do not touch any other note.
"
elif [ "$FORCE" -eq 1 ]; then
  EXTRA_NOTES="This is a re-ingest — update the existing summary and topic page, do not duplicate them.
"
fi
if [ -n "$NOTE" ]; then
  EXTRA_NOTES="${EXTRA_NOTES}${NOTE}
"
fi

# Topics mode: the table the LLM chooses from, rendered from topics.md via
# wiki-meta so the prompt sees exactly what the guard will validate against. A
# topics.md that fails validation is a configuration error — stop here, before
# the LLM call, with wiki-meta's message (it names the offending row).
TOPICS_RULE=""
if [ "$TOPICS_MODE" -eq 1 ]; then
  set +e; topics_tsv=$("$SCRIPT_DIR/wiki-meta" topics --wiki "$WT"); trc=$?; set -e
  if [ "$trc" -ne 0 ]; then
    echo "wiki-ingest-run: topics.md in $WIKI failed validation (wiki-meta rc=$trc) — fix it before ingesting" >&2
    exit 1
  fi
  TOPICS_TABLE=$(printf '%s\n' "$topics_tsv" | awk -F'\t' '
    BEGIN { print "| slug | title | scope |"; print "|---|---|---|" }
    NF >= 3 { print "| " $1 " | " $2 " | " $3 " |" }')
  TOPICS_RULE="TOPICS — every source in this wiki is filed under one or two fixed topics.
This is the complete list, from topics.md; choose from it and nothing else:

$TOPICS_TABLE

Pick ONE primary topic (the best fit for what the source is mainly about) and
AT MOST ONE secondary topic. Use misc only when nothing else fits. Write the
slugs (the first column, not the titles) in summary/$SLUG.md's frontmatter as
a block list, primary first, exactly in this form:

topics:
  - primary-slug
  - secondary-slug

Never invent a slug, and never edit topics.md. Never create or edit anything
under topic/: those are compiled topic pages, rebuilt from all their sources by
a separate step, and an ingest that writes there is rejected."
fi

# --- Run the LLM CLI ------------------------------------------------------------

# $CLI (default: claude) runs through wiki-agent with a tool allowlist as a
# real guardrail (claude --allowedTools, pi --tools) — no
# --dangerously-skip-permissions here. If a user points WIKI_INGEST_CLI at a
# wrapper that adds skip-permissions internally, that is their choice.
#
# An LLM failure must exit 1: exit codes 2 and 3 are reserved contract values
# (duplicate / no-changes) and the CLI's own exit code must never be mistaken
# for them.
llm_failed() {
  echo "wiki-ingest-run: LLM CLI ($CLI) failed for $INGEST_URL" >&2
  exit 1
}

# --- Single call (WIKI_INGEST_MODE=single): topics-mode article ingest ---------
# The agentic prompt's work in one request: the archive, the topics table, every
# note/topic title and the nearest notes' précis are inlined; the reply is
# summary.md and note.md between markers, and this script writes them plus the
# index.md entry and the log.md line the agent used to write. The staged-path
# guard, normalize_topics, the commit and the merge below then run unchanged.
# Measured 2026-09-13 (wiki-model-prompt-optimise SPEC-2): 10.9 s median model
# call on deepseek-4.1-flash at low effort; against the agentic incumbents the
# judge preferred these notes 8-4 on twelve articles.
single_ingest() {
  local scratch rc
  scratch="$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/wiki-ingest-single-XXXXXX")"
  SINGLE_SCRATCH="$scratch"
  {
    printf "The wiki's CLAUDE.md (project instructions for the wiki you are curating):\n\n"
    if [ -f "$WT/CLAUDE.md" ]; then cat "$WT/CLAUDE.md"; else printf '(none)\n'; fi
  } > "$scratch/system.md"
  NOTE_TITLES=$(WT="$WT" python3 -c '
import os, unicodedata
wt = os.environ["WT"]
t = set()
for d in ("note", "topic"):
    p = os.path.join(wt, d)
    if os.path.isdir(p):
        t.update(unicodedata.normalize("NFC", f[:-3]) for f in os.listdir(p) if f.endswith(".md"))
print("\n".join(sorted(t)))
')
  NEIGHBOURS=$("$SCRIPT_DIR/wiki-neighbours" --wiki "$WT" --source "$WT/raw/$SLUG.md")
  RAW_TEXT=$(cat "$WT/raw/$SLUG.md")
  cat > "$scratch/prompt.md" <<INGEST_SINGLE_EOF
You are curating one source into an Obsidian wiki. The source text has ALREADY
been fetched and saved verbatim to raw/$SLUG.md (frontmatter + body); its full
text is reproduced at the end of this message. Do NOT fetch anything.

The wiki CLAUDE.md (in your system prompt) defines page format and the layout:
raw/ = verbatim, summary/ = precis tagged with topics, note/ = one analysis
page per source, topic/ = compiled topic pages that you never write. Follow it.

Source URL: $INGEST_URL
$EXTRA_NOTES
STEP 0 — VERDICT (do this first): Read raw/$SLUG.md. Decide whether its body is
the real article/content, or a login wall, paywall teaser, cookie/consent page,
bot-check, or JavaScript app shell.
- If it is NOT real content (BLOCKED): respond with exactly the line
  === BLOCKED ===
  and nothing else.
- If it IS real content (CONTENT): continue.

$TOPICS_RULE

On CONTENT, produce:
1. summary/$SLUG.md — a concise precis (frontmatter with url/title/author/dates
   and the topics: block list described above, then 150 to 250 words in two or
   three short paragraphs). Same slug as the raw file.
2. note/<Title>.md — the analysis page, 700 to 1,100 words, in this order:
   - "## The argument in one paragraph": what the source claims and why it
     matters, stated so that it could be wrong (falsifiable), not a topic
     sentence.
   - "## Key quotes": at most FIVE, blockquoted, each with a line of commentary.
     Every quote must be copied VERBATIM from raw/$SLUG.md: no paraphrase in
     quotation marks, no tidying.
   - "## Critical analysis": opinionated, and earned by the text: say what is
     non-obvious, what is weak, and what the source leaves out.
   - "## Related": the RELATE links (item 3), one bullet per link.
   - the source footer linking [[raw/$SLUG]] and [[summary/$SLUG]].
   No key-themes or tags list: the topics frontmatter already classifies the
   source. Use the list of existing note/ and topic/ titles below for
   cross-link targets. <Title> must be a title that is not already in that
   list; if it is, pick a more specific title.
3. RELATE — connect this source to the wiki from YOUR OWN note. Find the 2–4
   MOST-related existing pages under note/ or topic/ (from the title list below).
   Under "## Related", give each its own bullet: the [[wikilink]], then ONE
   sentence that says specifically whether this source strengthens, nuances or
   complicates that page, and how. A bullet with no such sentence is a failure.
   Link only to titles that appear in the list, spelled exactly. The "Nearest
   existing notes" block gives the précis of the notes most similar to this
   source: use it to make each connection specific (what that page claims, and
   how this source bears on it). Any title in the full list may be linked.

OUTPUT — return both files in one response, delimited exactly like this, with
nothing before the first marker and nothing after the last:

=== FILE: summary.md ===
---
url: <exact url>
title: "<source title>"
author: <name, or omit the line>
date_fetched: <copied from raw/$SLUG.md>
date_published: <if stated, else omit the line>
topics:
  - <primary-slug>
  - <secondary-slug, or omit the line>
---

<precis: a few short paragraphs>
=== FILE: note.md ===
# <Title>

<the analysis page described in 2 and 3, ending with the footer
*Sources: [[raw/$SLUG]], [[summary/$SLUG]]*>
=== END ===

BEFORE YOU FINISH — output checklist (do not skip this):
- [ ] summary.md is present. This is item 1 above and the most commonly
      dropped output. Without it the caller REJECTS the whole ingest.
- [ ] summary.md's frontmatter has topics: — one or two slugs from the
      table, block form, primary first.
- [ ] Exactly ONE note: note.md, starting with "# <Title>", a title that is not
      in the existing-title list.

Guidelines:
- No preamble: your response starts with the first === FILE marker.
- Think briefly: the article is the evidence; do not deliberate at length.
- Preserve the author's voice when quoting; be opinionated in analysis.
- Keep pages phone-readable: short paragraphs, clear headers.
- Today's date is $INGEST_DATE.

---

# Nearest existing notes (similarity search over note/; exact title — its one-paragraph précis)

$NEIGHBOURS

---

# Existing note/ and topic/ page titles (one per line)

$NOTE_TITLES

---

# raw/$SLUG.md

$RAW_TEXT
INGEST_SINGLE_EOF
  unset NOTE_TITLES NEIGHBOURS RAW_TEXT
  set +e
  "$LLM" --system "$scratch/system.md" \
    --model "${WIKI_INGEST_MODEL:-deepseek-4.1-flash-background}" \
    --effort "${WIKI_INGEST_EFFORT:-low}" \
    --max-tokens "${WIKI_INGEST_MAX_TOKENS:-16000}" \
    < "$scratch/prompt.md" > "$scratch/reply.md"
  rc=$?
  set -e
  if [ "$rc" -eq 4 ]; then
    echo "wiki-ingest-run: the reply was cut off at max_tokens for $INGEST_URL; nothing written" >&2
    exit 1
  fi
  [ "$rc" -eq 0 ] || llm_failed
  # Write the files. BLOCKED removes the staged archive, which the empty-diff
  # check below turns into exit 3, exactly as when the agent ran rm.
  # NB: single-quoted program, so no single quotes inside it.
  set +e
  REPLY="$scratch/reply.md" WT="$WT" SLUG="$SLUG" URL="$INGEST_URL" DATE="$INGEST_DATE" \
  TOPICS_TSV="$topics_tsv" python3 -c '
import os, re, sys
e = os.environ
wt, slug, url, date = e["WT"], e["SLUG"], e["URL"], e["DATE"]
def die(msg):
    sys.stderr.write("wiki-ingest-run: single-call reply for " + url + ": " + msg + "\n")
    sys.exit(1)
t = open(e["REPLY"], encoding="utf-8", errors="replace").read()
t = re.sub(r"^\s*<think>.*?</think>\s*", "", t, flags=re.S)
if re.search(r"^=== BLOCKED ===\s*$", t, re.M) and "=== FILE:" not in t:
    os.remove(os.path.join(wt, "raw", slug + ".md"))
    print("BLOCKED")
    sys.exit(0)
ms = re.search(r"^=== FILE: summary(?:/[^=\n]*)?\.md ===[ \t]*$", t, re.M)
mn = re.search(r"^=== FILE: note(?:/[^=\n]*)?\.md ===[ \t]*$", t, re.M)
me = re.search(r"^=== END ===[ \t]*$", t, re.M)
if not (ms and mn and ms.start() < mn.start()):
    die("no === FILE: summary.md === and === FILE: note.md === markers")
summary = t[ms.end():mn.start()].strip("\n").strip() + "\n"
end = me.start() if me and me.start() > mn.start() else len(t)
note = re.sub(r"\n```\s*$", "", t[mn.end():end].strip("\n")).strip() + "\n"
h = re.search(r"^#[ \t]+(.+?)[ \t]*$", note, re.M)
if not summary.strip() or not h:
    die("empty summary, or a note with no # title")
# A title is a filename and a link target: keep it to what both allow.
title = re.sub(r"\s*:\s*", " — ", h.group(1))
title = re.sub(r"[\\/*?\"<>|#^\[\]]", "-", title)
title = re.sub(r"\s+", " ", title).strip(" .-")
if not title:
    die("the note title is empty once made filename-safe")
note = note[:h.start()] + "# " + title + note[h.end():]
for d in ("note", "topic"):
    if os.path.exists(os.path.join(wt, d, title + ".md")):
        die(d + "/" + title + ".md already exists; a new source needs a new note")
os.makedirs(os.path.join(wt, "summary"), exist_ok=True)
os.makedirs(os.path.join(wt, "note"), exist_ok=True)
open(os.path.join(wt, "summary", slug + ".md"), "w", encoding="utf-8").write(summary)
open(os.path.join(wt, "note", title + ".md"), "w", encoding="utf-8").write(note)
# Frontmatter facts for the index and log lines.
fm = ""
if summary.startswith("---\n") and "\n---\n" in summary[4:]:
    fm, body = summary[4:].split("\n---\n", 1)
else:
    body = summary
def field(k):
    m = re.search(r"^" + k + r":[ \t]*(.*)$", fm, re.M)
    v = m.group(1).strip() if m else ""
    return v[1:-1] if len(v) > 1 and v[0] == v[-1] and v[0] in "\"" else v
tm = re.search(r"^topics:[ \t]*\n((?:[ \t]+-[ \t]+.*\n?)+)", fm, re.M)
primary = re.findall(r"-[ \t]+(\S+)", tm.group(1))[0] if tm else ""
titles = dict(l.split("\t")[:2] for l in e["TOPICS_TSV"].splitlines() if l.count("\t") >= 2)
section = titles.get(primary) or titles.get("misc") or "Miscellany"
def sentences(text, n, cap):
    para = next((p for p in re.split(r"\n\s*\n", text) if p.strip() and not p.strip().startswith(("#", ">", "---"))), "")
    para = " ".join(para.split())
    s = " ".join(re.split(r"(?<=[.!?])\s+", para)[:n])
    return s if len(s) <= cap else s[:cap].rsplit(" ", 1)[0] + "…"
note_body = note[h.start():].split("\n", 1)[1] if "\n" in note[h.start():] else ""
entry = "- [[%s]] — %s" % (title, sentences(note_body, 1, 220) or sentences(body, 1, 220))
ip = os.path.join(wt, "index.md")
idx = open(ip, encoding="utf-8").read() if os.path.exists(ip) else "# Wiki Index\n"
lines = idx.rstrip("\n").split("\n")
at = next((i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.strip() == "## " + section), None)
if at is None:
    lines += ["", "## " + section, "", entry]
else:
    j = at + 1
    while j < len(lines) and not lines[j].startswith("## "):
        j += 1
    k = j
    while k > at + 1 and not lines[k - 1].strip():
        k -= 1
    lines[k:k] = [entry] if k > at + 1 else ["", entry]
open(ip, "w", encoding="utf-8").write("\n".join(lines) + "\n")
related = []
for x in re.findall(r"\[\[([^\]\[]+?)\]\]", note):
    x = x.split("|")[0].split("#")[0].strip()
    if not x.startswith(("raw/", "summary/")) and x not in related:
        related.append(x)
host = re.sub(r"^www\.", "", re.sub(r"^[a-z]+://", "", url).split("/")[0])
logline = "- %s: Ingested [%s](%s) (%s, %s, %s) — %s → raw/%s.md, [[%s]]. Cross-links: %s." % (
    date, field("title") or title, url, field("author") or "author not stated", host,
    field("date_published") or "publication date not stated", sentences(body, 3, 600), slug, title,
    ", ".join("[[" + r + "]]" for r in related[:4]) or "none")
lp = os.path.join(wt, "log.md")
log = open(lp, encoding="utf-8").read() if os.path.exists(lp) else ""
if log and not log.endswith("\n"):
    log += "\n"
open(lp, "w", encoding="utf-8").write(log + logline + "\n")
print("WROTE note/" + title + ".md")
'
  rc=$?
  set -e
  [ "$rc" -eq 0 ] || exit 1
}

# $CLI MUST run with the worktree as CWD: with the caller's CWD it picks up
# whatever project CLAUDE.md lives there and can start recursively
# orchestrating the pipeline (observed 2026-07-05). The in-prompt guardrails
# below reinforce this.
#
# Each mode has a topics-mode prompt and a legacy prompt. They are separate
# heredocs on purpose: the legacy text must stay byte-identical until every
# wiki has migrated, and sharing paragraphs between the two would make a
# topics-mode edit silently change the legacy prompt.
if [ "$SUMMARY_ONLY" -eq 1 ] && [ "$TOPICS_MODE" -eq 1 ]; then
  cat <<INGEST_EOF | (cd "$WT" && "$AGENT" --tools Read,Write --context "$WT") || llm_failed
You are backfilling ONE missing precis in an Obsidian wiki. The source was
ingested previously and its verbatim text is already archived at raw/$SLUG.md.
Do NOT fetch anything. Do NOT use WebFetch, WebSearch, or any browser tool.

Wiki location: $WT
Source archive: raw/$SLUG.md

Read raw/$SLUG.md and write EXACTLY ONE file: summary/$SLUG.md — a concise
precis of that source, in the curated format the wiki CLAUDE.md defines.

It starts with YAML frontmatter, then the precis:

---
url: <copy the url: value from raw/$SLUG.md's frontmatter, exactly>
title: "<the source's own title>"
author: <author name>
date_fetched: <copy the date_fetched: value from raw/$SLUG.md>
date_published: <YYYY-MM-DD, if the source states one>
topics:
  - <primary topic slug>
  - <secondary topic slug, only if one genuinely applies>
---

Omit title, author or date_published only if the archived text genuinely does
not give you the value — never invent one. url and date_fetched are copied from
the raw file, so they are always available. topics: is required.

$TOPICS_RULE

Below the frontmatter: a few short paragraphs saying what the source covers, its
main claims, and anything notable. Phone-readable — short paragraphs, no
preamble. This is a precis, not a copy: do not reproduce the source at length.

HARD CONSTRAINTS — this is a backfill of an already-ingested source, not a new
ingest. The source is already in index.md and log.md and already has its
analysis note; re-logging or re-indexing it would duplicate those entries.
- Write summary/$SLUG.md and NOTHING ELSE. One file.
- Do NOT edit or delete raw/$SLUG.md.
- Do NOT create or edit anything under note/ or topic/.
- Do NOT touch index.md, log.md, topics.md, or any file at the wiki root.
- Do NOT run git branch/commit/merge/push — the caller owns all git.
- Today's date is $INGEST_DATE.
INGEST_EOF
