On CONTENT, produce:
1. summary/$SLUG.md — a concise precis (frontmatter with url/title/author/dates
   + a few short paragraphs). Same slug as the raw file.
2. topic/<Title>.md — the analysis page: one-paragraph precis, key quotes
   (blockquoted, with commentary), key themes (#concept #tool #pattern #person),
   opinionated critical analysis, [[wikilinks]] to related pages, source footer
   linking [[raw/$SLUG]] and [[summary/$SLUG]]. Read index.md for cross-link
   targets and grep existing topic pages for related keywords.
3. RELATE — connect this source to the wiki from YOUR OWN page. Find the 2–4
   MOST-related existing topic/ pages (use index.md and grep) and link to each
   with a [[wikilink]] from the page you just wrote, in a sentence that says how
   this source strengthens, nuances, or complicates that page.

   Do NOT edit any existing topic/ page. Not even additively. Cross-page
   curation is a SEPARATE COMPILE STEP (wiki-recompile), which rebuilds a theme
   page from ALL of its sources at once and can therefore revise stale claims
   instead of only appending to them. Editing shared pages from inside a
   per-source ingest is what produced this wiki's merge conflicts and its
   un-revisable hub pages; the link you write above carries the same
   information, and Obsidian derives the backlink for free.
4. Update index.md — add the topic page under the most appropriate section.
5. Append to log.md — exactly ONE bullet line, EXACTLY this format:
   - $INGEST_DATE: Ingested [Title]($INGEST_URL) (author, site, publication-date) — 1–3 sentence summary. → raw/$SLUG.md, [[Page Title]]. Cross-links: [[A]], [[B]].

BEFORE YOU FINISH — output checklist (do not skip this). Check each on disk:
- [ ] summary/$SLUG.md EXISTS. This is item 1 above and the most commonly
      dropped output. Without it the caller REJECTS the whole ingest.
- [ ] The analysis page is at topic/<Title>.md — INSIDE the topic/ directory.
      NOT <Title>.md at the wiki root. A root-written page fails the ingest.
- [ ] raw/$SLUG.md is unchanged (verbatim source, never rewritten).
- [ ] index.md has the new entry; log.md has exactly one new bullet.

Write NOTHING to the wiki root. The ONLY root files you may touch are index.md
and log.md. Every page you create belongs in summary/ or topic/.

Guidelines:
- Preserve the author's voice when quoting; be opinionated in analysis.
- Keep pages phone-readable: short paragraphs, clear headers.
- Edits to existing pages must be additive and surgical — never remove another
  page's content.
- Today's date is $INGEST_DATE.
INGEST_EOF
fi

# --- Commit --------------------------------------------------------------------

git -C "$WT" add -A

# BLOCKED verdict: the LLM deleted the staged raw/$SLUG.md and wrote nothing,
# so there is no net change → treat as fetch failure (exit 3 → surf). CONTENT
# verdict: summary/ + topic/ (and index/log) are present → commit all tiers.
if git -C "$WT" diff --cached --quiet; then
  if [ "$SUMMARY_ONLY" -eq 1 ]; then
    # Not a fetch failure, so not exit 3 (which tells the orchestrator to retry
    # with surf) — the archive is right here and the LLM simply produced nothing.
    echo "wiki-ingest-run: --summary-only wrote nothing for raw/$SLUG.md" >&2
    exit 1
  fi
  echo "NO CHANGES — blocked or empty for $INGEST_URL"
  exit 3
fi

# Backfill guard: exactly the missing precis, and nothing else. A backfill that
# re-logs or re-indexes an already-ingested source duplicates those entries.
if [ "$SUMMARY_ONLY" -eq 1 ]; then
  STAGED=$(git -C "$WT" diff --cached --name-only)
  if ! printf '%s\n' "$STAGED" | grep -q "^summary/${SLUG}\.md\$"; then
    echo "wiki-ingest-run: --summary-only wrote no summary/$SLUG.md" >&2
    exit 1
  fi
  OUTSIDE=$(printf '%s\n' "$STAGED" | grep -v '^summary/' || true)
  if [ -n "$OUTSIDE" ]; then
    echo "wiki-ingest-run: --summary-only touched files outside summary/ for $SLUG: $(printf '%s' "$OUTSIDE" | tr '\n' ' ')" >&2
    exit 1
  fi
fi

# Appended to the commit subject when the guard repaired topics: (below), so
# the repair is on the record rather than silent. Empty in legacy mode.
COMMIT_NOTE=""

# normalize_topics — repair summary/$SLUG.md's topics: in place and re-stage it.
# wiki-meta exits 0 when the list was already right, 1 when it rewrote the key
# (title → slug, case, dedupe, truncate, flow → block, missing → misc), 2 on an
# error (unreadable file, broken topics.md). A repair is NOT a rejection: the
# raw, summary and note are intact and valuable, and throwing away a
# five-minute LLM run for a metadata slip is the wrong trade; the audit reports
# repairs so they are not invisible. A missing summary still rejects above.
normalize_topics() {
  local nrc
  set +e
  "$SCRIPT_DIR/wiki-meta" normalize-topics --wiki "$WT" "$WT/summary/$SLUG.md" >&2
  nrc=$?
  set -e
  case "$nrc" in
    0) : ;;
    1) git -C "$WT" add -- "summary/$SLUG.md"
       COMMIT_NOTE=" (topics repaired)" ;;
    *) echo "wiki-ingest-run: could not validate topics: in summary/$SLUG.md (wiki-meta rc=$nrc) — refusing to commit" >&2
       exit 1 ;;
  esac
}

if [ "$SUMMARY_ONLY" -eq 1 ] && [ "$TOPICS_MODE" -eq 1 ]; then
  normalize_topics
fi

# Guard: a CONTENT result must include a summary AND an analysis page. Check the
# STAGED PATHS, not the filesystem — $WT is a worktree of the whole wiki, so a
# glob like "$WT/summary/"*.md matches hundreds of pre-existing files and can
# never fail (kata x04s: that masked a dead summary/ tier for 32 ingests).
if [ "${VERBATIM_ONLY:-0}" -ne 1 ] && [ "$SUMMARY_ONLY" -ne 1 ]; then
  STAGED=$(git -C "$WT" diff --cached --name-only)

  # summary/ is per-source, so it must be exactly this slug.
  if ! printf '%s\n' "$STAGED" | grep -q "^summary/${SLUG}\.md\$"; then
    echo "wiki-ingest-run: incomplete result — no summary/$SLUG.md staged for $INGEST_URL" >&2
    exit 1
  fi

  ROOT_ALLOW='index|log|ingest-queue|CLAUDE'
  if [ "$TOPICS_MODE" -eq 1 ]; then
    # Topics mode. The analysis page is note/<Title>.md and topic/ holds only
    # compiled pages, so the legacy "some topic/ path is staged" check inverts:
    # any topic/ write is a hard failure, and the note requirement is exact.
    #
    # core.quotePath=false and --no-renames are both load-bearing. Note titles
    # carry em-dashes and accents, and git C-quotes such paths by default, so a
    # quoted name would never match the plain path we read back from HEAD.
    # Rename detection would fold "delete note A, add note B" into one R entry
    # and let an overwrite-by-rename through the one-note count; with it off
    # that is two paths and is rejected.
    ROOT_ALLOW="$ROOT_ALLOW|topics"
    STAGED=$(git -C "$WT" -c core.quotePath=false diff --cached --name-only --no-renames)

    if printf '%s\n' "$STAGED" | grep -q '^topic/'; then
      echo "wiki-ingest-run: wrote under topic/ for $INGEST_URL: $(printf '%s\n' "$STAGED" | grep '^topic/' | tr '\n' ' ')" >&2
      echo "wiki-ingest-run: topic/ holds only compiled pages (wiki-compile writes them); the analysis page belongs in note/ — refusing to commit" >&2
      exit 1
    fi
    if printf '%s\n' "$STAGED" | grep -qx 'topics.md'; then
      echo "wiki-ingest-run: topics.md was edited during the ingest of $INGEST_URL — the topic list changes only by hand; refusing to commit" >&2
      exit 1
    fi

    NOTE_PATHS=$(printf '%s\n' "$STAGED" | grep '^note/' || true)
    NOTE_COUNT=$(printf '%s\n' "$NOTE_PATHS" | sed '/^$/d' | wc -l | tr -d ' ')
    if [ "$NOTE_COUNT" -eq 0 ]; then
      echo "wiki-ingest-run: incomplete result — no note/ page staged for $INGEST_URL" >&2
      exit 1
    fi
    if [ "$NOTE_COUNT" -ne 1 ]; then
      echo "wiki-ingest-run: $NOTE_COUNT note/ paths staged for $INGEST_URL, expected exactly one: $(printf '%s' "$NOTE_PATHS" | tr '\n' ' ')" >&2
      echo "wiki-ingest-run: an ingest writes its own note and touches no other — refusing to commit" >&2
      exit 1
    fi
    NOTE_PATH="$NOTE_PATHS"

    # The one note must be NEW. A modified note means the LLM wrote over a page
    # that already existed (kata 6ctn). The only legitimate modification is a
    # --force re-ingest updating the note a previous ingest of THIS source
    # wrote, which is recognised by its footer at HEAD citing this slug's raw/
    # or summary/ — not by title, which is what the LLM got wrong.
    if ! git -C "$WT" -c core.quotePath=false diff --cached --name-only --no-renames --diff-filter=A \
        | grep -qxF "$NOTE_PATH"; then
      if [ "$FORCE" -ne 1 ]; then
        echo "wiki-ingest-run: $NOTE_PATH already exists and was modified during the ingest of $INGEST_URL" >&2
        echo "wiki-ingest-run: a new source gets a new note; pick a title that is not taken — refusing to commit" >&2
        exit 1
      fi
      if ! git -C "$WT" show "HEAD:$NOTE_PATH" 2>/dev/null \
          | grep -qE "(raw|summary)/${SLUG}(\]\]|[|#])"; then
        echo "wiki-ingest-run: --force re-ingest of $INGEST_URL modified $NOTE_PATH, whose footer does not cite raw/$SLUG or summary/$SLUG" >&2
        echo "wiki-ingest-run: that note belongs to a different source — refusing to commit" >&2
        exit 1
      fi
    fi
  else
    # topic/ is a prefix match on purpose: topic filenames are human titles, not
    # slugs, and one ingest may legitimately touch several topic pages. A page
    # written to the wiki root instead of topic/ fails here, which is the point.
    if ! printf '%s\n' "$STAGED" | grep -q '^topic/'; then
      echo "wiki-ingest-run: incomplete result — no topic/ page staged for $INGEST_URL" >&2
      exit 1
    fi
  fi

  # No NEW top-level *.md outside the known set (kata 25nm: repo-mode sometimes
  # writes "<Title>.md" to the wiki root, and Obsidian wikilinks resolve by
  # filename so nothing visibly breaks).
  STRAY=$(git -C "$WT" diff --cached --name-only --diff-filter=A \
    | grep -E '^[^/]+\.md$' \
    | grep -v -E "^($ROOT_ALLOW)\.md$" || true)
  if [ -n "$STRAY" ]; then
    echo "wiki-ingest-run: wrote new file(s) to the wiki root for $INGEST_URL: $(printf '%s' "$STRAY" | tr '\n' ' ')" >&2
    if [ "$TOPICS_MODE" -eq 1 ]; then
      echo "wiki-ingest-run: analysis pages belong in note/, precis in summary/ — refusing to commit" >&2
    else
      echo "wiki-ingest-run: topic pages belong in topic/, precis in summary/ — refusing to commit" >&2
    fi
    exit 1
  fi

  # Last: the structural checks above decide whether there is anything worth
  # committing; only then is the metadata on it repaired.
  if [ "$TOPICS_MODE" -eq 1 ]; then
    normalize_topics
  fi
fi
if [ "$SUMMARY_ONLY" -eq 1 ]; then
  git -C "$WT" commit -m "Backfill summary: $SLUG$COMMIT_NOTE" --author="wiki-ingest <noreply@wiki-ingest>"
elif [ "$REPO_MODE" -eq 1 ]; then
  git -C "$WT" commit -m "Ingest (repo analysis): $INGEST_URL$COMMIT_NOTE" --author="wiki-ingest <noreply@wiki-ingest>"
else
  git -C "$WT" commit -m "Ingest: $INGEST_URL$COMMIT_NOTE" --author="wiki-ingest <noreply@wiki-ingest>"
fi

# Refuse to auto-commit into a repo that is mid-operation. This MUST run before
# the `git add -A` below: add -A marks conflicted paths resolved, after which
# `git ls-files -u` is empty and the evidence is gone, and the commit then
# concludes someone else's merge with their unresolved tree in it (kata cntt).
# Exit rather than skip: skipping leaves MERGE_HEAD set, and merge_with_retry's
# `git merge --abort` would then destroy the captain's hand-resolution.
INPROGRESS=$(inprogress_ops)
if [ -n "$INPROGRESS" ]; then
  echo "wiki-ingest-run: $WIKI has a git operation in progress ($INPROGRESS) — refusing to auto-commit" >&2
  echo "wiki-ingest-run: finish or abort it, then re-run. Branch $BRANCH kept for retry." >&2
  exit 1
fi
# --diff-filter=U rather than `ls-files -u`: same detection, one line per path.
UNMERGED=$(git -C "$WIKI" diff --name-only --diff-filter=U 2>/dev/null || true)
if [ -n "$UNMERGED" ]; then
  echo "wiki-ingest-run: $WIKI has unmerged paths — refusing to auto-commit: $(printf '%s' "$UNMERGED" | tr '\n' ' ')" >&2
  echo "wiki-ingest-run: branch $BRANCH kept for retry." >&2
  exit 1
fi

# Commit any local changes on main first (e.g. Obsidian edits) so merge doesn't fail
git -C "$WIKI" add -A 2>/dev/null || true

# Belt and braces: never commit conflict markers, even with no operation flagged
# in progress. Anchored on the <<<<<<< / >>>>>>> forms only — a bare "=======" is
# a legal setext heading underline in markdown and false-positives across a wiki.
# `while IFS= read -r`, not a for loop: topic filenames contain spaces.
# core.quotePath=false is load-bearing, not cosmetic: by default git C-quotes any
# path with a non-ASCII byte, and `git show ":$p"` on that quoted name resolves
# to nothing, fails, and the failure is swallowed by the 2>/dev/null below — the
# scan silently cannot fire. The wiki separates title from subtitle with an
# em-dash (U+2014), so this is ~80 of its 991 topic pages, not an edge case.
MARKED=""
while IFS= read -r p; do
  [ -n "$p" ] || continue
  if git -C "$WIKI" show ":$p" 2>/dev/null | grep -qE '^(<<<<<<<|>>>>>>>) '; then
    MARKED="$MARKED$p
"
  fi
done < <(git -C "$WIKI" -c core.quotePath=false diff --cached --name-only)
if [ -n "$MARKED" ]; then
  echo "wiki-ingest-run: conflict markers in staged file(s) — refusing to auto-commit: $(printf '%s' "$MARKED" | tr '\n' ' ')" >&2
  # Unstage what the add -A above staged; file contents are untouched. Only
  # reachable when no operation is in progress, i.e. nothing was carefully staged.
  git -C "$WIKI" reset --quiet 2>/dev/null || true
  echo "wiki-ingest-run: branch $BRANCH kept for retry." >&2
  exit 1
fi

git -C "$WIKI" diff --cached --quiet 2>/dev/null || \
  git -C "$WIKI" commit -m "Auto-commit local changes before ingest merge" 2>/dev/null || true

# --- Merge into main (with retry) + push ----------------------------------------

set +e; merge_with_retry "$WIKI"; mrc=$?; set -e
if [ "$mrc" -eq 3 ]; then
  echo "wiki-ingest-run: $INGEST_URL collided with a peer ingest that merged first — add/add on: $(printf '%s' "$MERGE_COLLISIONS" | tr '\n' '|' | sed 's/|/, /g')" >&2
  reruns="${WIKI_INGEST_COLLISION_RERUN:-0}"
  case "$reruns" in ''|*[!0-9]*) reruns=0 ;; esac
  # --summary-only writes summary/<slug>.md for an archive that already exists,
  # so its one add/add is a peer backfilling the same source at the same time:
  # the precis is there now, and a re-run would only overwrite it.
  if [ "$SUMMARY_ONLY" -eq 1 ]; then
    echo "MERGE FAILED for $INGEST_URL: a peer backfilled summary/$SLUG.md first — branch $BRANCH kept" >&2
    exit 1
  fi
  if [ "$reruns" -lt 2 ]; then
    echo "wiki-ingest-run: slug/title collision — re-running $INGEST_URL from a fresh worktree off main (re-run $((reruns + 1)) of 2)" >&2
    # Our branch is superseded by the re-run. cleanup removes the worktree first
    # (a checked-out branch cannot be deleted); the EXIT trap runs it again and
    # every step tolerates what is already gone. The child picks its own
    # branch and worktree names ($$), which the parent's cleanup never names.
    cleanup
    git -C "$WIKI" branch -D "$BRANCH" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
    set +e
    WIKI_INGEST_COLLISION_RERUN=$((reruns + 1)) "$BASH" "$SCRIPT_DIR/$(basename "$0")" ${ORIG_ARGV[@]+"${ORIG_ARGV[@]}"}
    crc=$?
    set -e
    exit "$crc"
  fi
  echo "MERGE FAILED for $INGEST_URL: slug/title collision with peer ingests persisted through $reruns re-runs — branch $BRANCH kept for retry" >&2
  exit 1
elif [ "$mrc" -ne 0 ]; then
  echo "MERGE FAILED after 5 attempts for $INGEST_URL — branch $BRANCH kept for retry" >&2
  exit 1
fi

# Push, catching up with origin when another writer got there first: a
# rejected push usually means origin/main moved on since sync_with_origin (or a
# CI clone raced another runner). Fetch it, merge it into main (index.md and
# log.md are merge=union, so concurrent appends merge clean), and push again —
# up to 3 pushes. The merge follows the shared rules above. A content conflict
# with origin is aborted at once and the local commit stays on main, unpushed:
# push-failed. No origin remote, a failed fetch, or a rejection that is not
# about history (origin/main already in main) all stop at the first failed
# push, exactly as the old single push.
push_with_sync() {
  local attempt=1 mrc
  while :; do
    if git -C "$WIKI" push origin main --quiet 2>/dev/null; then
      return 0
    fi
    [ "$attempt" -lt 3 ] || return 1
    attempt=$((attempt + 1))
    fetch_origin_main || return 1
    if git -C "$WIKI" merge-base --is-ancestor "$ORIGIN_SHA" main 2>/dev/null; then
      return 1   # nothing to catch up on: the rejection was not a race
    fi
    echo "wiki-ingest-run: push rejected — merging origin/main ($ORIGIN_SHA) into main and retrying" >&2
    merge_origin_sha "Merge origin/main into main before push" && mrc=0 || mrc=$?
    case "$mrc" in
      0) continue ;;
      2) echo "wiki-ingest-run: $SYNC_WHY — merge aborted, local commit kept unpushed" >&2
         return 1 ;;
    esac
    # The merge never started: wait, as merge_with_retry does, and spend an attempt.
    sleep 3
  done
}

if push_with_sync; then
  PUSH_STATUS="pushed"
else
  PUSH_STATUS="push-failed"
fi

if [ "$SUMMARY_ONLY" -eq 1 ]; then
  echo "SUMMARY BACKFILLED: summary/$SLUG.md (branch $BRANCH, merged, $PUSH_STATUS)"
else
  echo "INGESTED: $INGEST_URL (branch $BRANCH, merged, $PUSH_STATUS)"
fi
# Strict mode for a writer with nowhere else to keep its commit (a CI runner's
# throwaway clone): an unpushed ingest is a lost ingest, so say so in the exit
# code. Off by default — the Mac's launchd job keeps the commit locally and
# relies on exit 0.
if [ "$PUSH_STATUS" = "push-failed" ] && [ "${WIKI_INGEST_REQUIRE_PUSH:-0}" = 1 ]; then
  echo "wiki-ingest-run: WIKI_INGEST_REQUIRE_PUSH=1 and the push failed — exit 5" >&2
  exit 5
fi
# trap removes the worktree and the (now merged) branch
